@mcraj017 @Karm  Hi! This issue appears because the implementation in Graal Native Image does not currently implement a mechanism for events that are larger than the thread local buffer (default 8192 kb). In HotSpot, the algorithm would either lease a global buffer temporarily for the write, if it can fit, or attempt to allocate a transient buffer (e.g. via malloc) that can fulfill the write request.

At the moment, the expectation is that these events are safely discarded and the program continues to run. The full solution here would be to implement a similar algorithm to support writes of arbitrary size.

If you'd like to see the HotSpot algorithm, you can follow the implementation of this flush method: https://github.com/openjdk/jdk/blob/master/src/hotspot/share/jfr/writers/jfrJavaEventWriter.cpp#L136
